  "result": "I wrote the 10-minute lesson on O3 (context and memory) and a five-item quiz with its key. I haven't opened the lesson in a browser, so its practice buttons are untested. I estimated the length by hand (about 1,400 words, roughly 9 to 10 minutes). It may land a little short of the 150-words-a-minute target.\n\n**Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory.html`\n- It starts with a game-backpack picture of the context window, with a worked example of why cost grows on every step.\n- It then separates what lasts one step, one session or many sessions.\n- It covers retrieval (searching the manuals for the right passages) and saved notes, each with a worked example drawn from the makerspace assistant.\n- It names the common mix-up that a bigger window gives long-term memory.\n- Practice is three short checks, one of them a placement exercise for the assistant.\n- The main source is Anthropic's [context engineering article](https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-context-engineering-for-ai-agents).\n\n**Quiz:** `quizzes/0002.json` (key in `keys/0002.json`) is ready when you want to take it.\n\n**Other files:**\n- `RESOURCES.md` is new and lists the two Anthropic sources I used.\n- `NOTES.md` now records the three new misconception ids M7 to M9.\n- I didn't write a cheat sheet this time.\n\nQuestion for you: do you want a cheat sheet on where each kind of information goes (context, retrieval or notes)? Ask me anything about the lesson in the chat.",
